{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>These are the records.</b> Why is המשכן said twice? Because it was destined to be taken as collateral twice — the first and second temples." "<b>The testimony.</b> That it is a testimony to the nations of the world that the Holy One, blessed be He, was appeased for the deed of the calf, for the Shekhinah dwells there. Another explanation: that it was a testimony for Moses, for at the time they suspected him of stealing shekels from the work of the Mishkan, Moses said to them: I want the Mishkan to be a testimony. And they went back and counted and found that they were put into the hooks for the pillars. And he derives it from ״המלאכה היתה דים״ — take the initial letters, and they go up to fifteen vavs, meaning fifteen extra. And immediately Moses gave fifteen praises to the Holy One, blessed be He, and they are in Yishtabach — שיר ושבחה — and corresponding to them, fifteen ברוך in ברוך שאמר, and corresponding to them, fifteen vavs in אמת ויציב etc." "<b>By Itamar.</b> Even though Moses our teacher was appointed over everything, he needed to appoint Itamar with him, because one does not appoint authority over the public with fewer than two."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:04:51.978443251Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}